  "_note": "Rows removed from data/leaderboard.json by PR #85 (issue #81) on 2026-09-19.",
  "_why": "All 19 were bulk X-username scans (URL templated as https://twitter.com/<handle> or https://x.com/<handle>) that hit the social-media guard and produced a limited-scan result. Each carried band=COMPROMISED and score 2-3, manufactured purely from AUTH-01's name-only partial credit (2.0 pts / ~116 max) on a site that was never assessed. That is a false-danger: a social-only agent is not 'compromised', it is UNRATED (no site to assess). Triage classified all 19 as group (b) 'genuinely no website / social-only' \u2014 0 fetch-failures, 0 ambiguous. The 0.12.0 persistence gate (rated=False scans are not ranked) prevents this class from ever being ranked again.",
  "_reversible": "This file preserves the removed rows verbatim. If any row is later found to be a legitimate rated entry, restore it into data/leaderboard.json. A social-only 'limited leaderboard' should be a deliberate product feature designed for that population \u2014 NOT relabelled bulk-scan residue.",
